#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:98
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Xfce4 Session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:101
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Xfce4 Session</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:105
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>./configure --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --sysconfdir=/etc   \\\n"
"            --disable-legacy-sm &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:111
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a test suite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:115
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:118
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:123
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:126
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--disable-legacy-sm</parameter>: This switch disables legacy "
"session management which isn't necessary on modern system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:134
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring Xfce4 Session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:137
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"There are several optional run time dependencies for "
"<application>Xfce4</application>: <xref linkend=\"dbus\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"gnupg2\"/>, <xref linkend=\"hicolor-icon-theme\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"openssh\"/>, and <xref linkend=\"xinit\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:147
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"When building an <application>Xfce4</application> package, some "
"configuration files are installed in <filename class=\"directory\"> "
"/usr/share/applications</filename>, <filename class=\"directory\"> "
"/usr/share/icons</filename>, and <filename class=\"directory\"> "
"/usr/share/mime</filename>. In order to use those files in your "
"<application>Xfce4</application> session, you need to update various "
"databases. Do that by running, as the <systemitem class=\"username\"> "
"root</systemitem> user (you need to have the recommended dependencies "
"installed):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:158
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>update-desktop-database &amp;&amp;\n"
"update-mime-database /usr/share/mime</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:163
#, xml-text
msgid "Starting Xfce4"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:166
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You can start <application>Xfce4</application> from runlevel 3, using <xref "
"linkend=\"xinit\"/>, or from runlevel 5, using a Display Manager, such as "
"<xref linkend=\"lightdm\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:172
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You can start <application>Xfce4</application> from a TTY using <xref "
"linkend=\"xinit\"/>, or from a graphical display manager, such as <xref "
"linkend=\"lightdm\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:178
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To start <application>Xfce4</application> using <xref linkend=\"xinit\"/>, "
"run the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#.  TODO: A plain "startxfce4" command works for me on Systemd.
#.          But maybe it does not work on SysV.  Need more investigate.
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:185
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; ~/.xinitrc &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>dbus-launch --exit-with-x11 startxfce4</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"startx</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:192
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The X session starts on the first unused virtual terminal, normally vt7.  "
"You can switch to another vt<emphasis>n</emphasis> simultaneously pressing "
"the keys Ctrl-Alt-F<emphasis>n</emphasis> (<emphasis>n</emphasis>=1, 2, "
"...).  To switch back to the X session, normally started at vt7, use Ctrl-"
"Alt-F7. The vt where the command <command>startx</command> was executed will"
" display many messages, including X starting messages, applications "
"automatically started with the session, and eventually, some warning and "
"error messages. You may prefer to redirect those messages to a log file, "
"which not only will keep the initial vt uncluttered, but can also be used "
"for debugging purposes. This can be done starting X with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:205
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>startx &amp;&gt; ~/.x-session-errors</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:209
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You may wish to drop dbus-launch, e.g., just using startxfce4 in ~/.xinitrc."
" However some capabilities such as mounting or umounting file systems from a"
" file manager will not be possible, or the reboot option will be absent or "
"inoperative, among other problems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xfce/core/xfce4-session.xml:217
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"When shutting down or rebooting, the shutdown messages appear on the vt "
"where X was running. If you wish to see those messages, simultaneously press"
" keys Alt-F7 (assuming that X was running on vt7)."
msgstr ""

